From 2654cc2ee02d0903cd78daf1cddb5d55224e769d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 02:40:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] feat(environment): baked light pools and floor by tier

One seeded CanvasTexture lightmap per floor zone: a warm pool per light
target (1.6 m, 0.3 m toward the aisle center, alpha 0.85, color by age),
door threshold pools and soft plinth contact patches. A shared 256 px
wall-wash scallop with 2 m seams on wash bays behind each target, tinted
per target and snapped to each wall line's seam grid. High tier floors use
one MeshReflectorMaterial pass shared by every zone; medium and low use the
library floor with the lightmap and no second pass. The pure light plan
(lightPlan, assignLights, matchLights, light levels, beam cones) lives in
lightPlan.ts; fixtures.ts becomes fixtureMatrices.ts without the desk block.

WP: WP-11
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016CcKJFMWCyXKspJx4YvMS7
